# 视频画风与动作 · 电影级半写实三维

## Storyboard compilation

Apply video_prefix.md to the target rendering while retaining the selected character designs.
Compile the supplied Shot, Camera and Action information; do not redesign the shot plan.
Preserve explicit source cuts and their timing; otherwise use one continuous shot.
Every actual cut needs its own shot heading under the selected model's syntax. Do not hide
an extra cut, reverse shot or montage inside one shot description.

## Action and state

Give the required framing and visible initial state, the principal supplied action and
its visible result. Describe body position, contact, support and force only where necessary
to make that action unambiguous. Start directly in the requested state, and retain it across
later shots until a supplied event changes it. The reference sheet's display pose and
incidental support objects are not action instructions.

Use short concrete sentences. Preserve who acts on whom and deliberate cause/effect;
do not turn an intentional action into an accident. Do not add gestures, impacts, injuries,
reactions, transitions or costume changes to enrich prose. Hair, fabric, weather and crowd
motion support the main action. Reuse stable subject labels rather than repeating static
face, clothing, material and background inventories.

## Camera and sound

Keep one feasible supplied camera path. Character 全景 means a full-body/full shot including
the feet and relevant support/contact points. Reserve environment-dominated wide views for
source 远景/大远景 or an explicit location introduction. Frame the local setting needed for
the action rather than copying an environment reference's whole-location composition.
Reconcile camera directions with body geometry while preserving the action and original timing.

Keep complete supplied dialogue, its speaker, language and event position. Speech and
necessary non-overlapping actions fit the supplied duration; do not invent faster delivery,
extend time or omit dialogue. Use concise synchronized physical sounds and continuous ambience;
include music only when supplied. Follow the selected model's output and reference syntax.
